/-  ZooDH.lean -- certified Davenport-Heilbronn diffraction (MIRRORMERE QC-B1).

    The DH analogue of BraggH100: the finite-volume diffraction amplitude of the
    Davenport-Heilbronn zero comb at two rational frequencies

        u2 = 693147/1000000 (~= log 2, BraggH100's frequency)
        u5 = 1609437/1000000 (~= log 5, natural for a period-5 object)

    DH is the classic RH counterexample class: a Dirichlet series with a Riemann-type
    functional equation but NO Euler product, hence zeros OFF the critical line.  This
    file certifies BOTH parts of its diffraction:

      * dh_diffraction_online_box_u{2,5} -- the ON-line ordinate sum sum cos(gamma_k·u)
        over the 52 on-line DH zeros with 0 < gamma_k <= 100 (winding-certified,
        dh_zeros.json), each cos enclosed by the CosEnclosure double-angle chain +
        Lipschitz bracket absorption.  DIRECT analogue of bragg_amplitude_h100.

      * dh_offline_term_box_u{2,5} -- the OFF-line pair's contribution
        2·cosh(delta·u)·cos(gamma·u), delta = beta - 1/2 != 0, for the certified
        off-line zero.  The cosh(delta·u) > 1 factor is the DISTINCTIVE off-line
        signature (an on-line zero has delta = 0 => cosh = 1 => a plain cos term).
        cosh enclosed by the local order-6 cosh_bracket (exp Taylor remainder).

    TRUST.  Bracket-membership / delta-value hypotheses carry the Arb inventory trust
    (dh_zeros.json winding certificates + Re-D sign bisection), same class as BraggH100's
    hLine.  Everything downstream is kernel-checked (no sorry).  conjecture1_proved = False.
-/
import Mathlib
import CosEnclosure

open Real

